      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's a debate, but it feels like the \"safety\" side always gets the benefit of the doubt in these talks. like, when people talk about facial recognition, they focus on how it catches criminals, but they don't usually talk about how it basically turns every citizen into a permanent suspect. don't u think the way these debates are framed is actually kind of biased toward the tech/security side?",
